# Reactive Surface Implementation Plan - 2026-07-05

## §0. Review Summary

- First implementation is BP-only, local-player-only, no multiplayer, no Water Plugin, no AnimNotify, no production C++.
- The actual local player owns `BP_ReactiveSurfaceControllerActor`.
- The controller collects source candidates once per update, then channels run with fully separated Niagara/RT/User parameter namespaces.
- Bone/socket components are passive `ReactivePoint` markers only; they must not tick.
- Ground Contact Sources drive Snow/Sand/Mud/Dust.
- Influence Sources drive Grass/Foliage and Water/Puddle.
- Ground uses one Ground RT; Snow/Sand use footprint mask texture stamps.
- Grass has no PhysMat gate; only opt-in materials sample Grass RT.
- Water/Puddle uses project-owned ripple RTs plus PuddleVolume + Weather MPC.
- Runtime Array DI must use `Custom HLSL input -> Module.* -> User.*`; hidden/direct `User.*` is banned.

