## §3. Risks / Remaining Validation

| Risk | Not covered by smoke | Phase | Fallback |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Snow indentation visual quality | Exact sole silhouette is secondary to a continuous, natural depression during planted or sliding foot motion; final depth/rim/material feel still requires user approval. | Phase 4 / visual tuning | Tune `RS_Ground_DragStampSpacingWS` and the Ground material without reverting to every-Tick injection or actor-center spacing. |
| Old footprint preservation feel | V4c proves movement/zero-fill, not player acceptance. | Phase 4 | Larger Ground window, chunk recenter, fade/clear fallback. |
| Water/Puddle solver | No production material normal/ripple quality test yet. | Phase 5 | Damped ripple first; fall back to simpler radial impulse. |
| Auxiliary per-source arrays | Position Array DI is proven; extra payload arrays are not locked. | Phase 3 | Uniform radius/strength or source-class splits. |
| Packaged-game collection cost | Editor smoke measured `0.337439-0.367008 ms`; packaged cost not measured. | Phase 3 / 7 | Reduce slot counts or update rate. |
| Parallel channel activation | 3RT always-active future smoke remains excluded. 2-channel Ground+Grass is unblocked on the production `activate(false)` path; `activate(true)` 2+ channel reset behavior remains a non-production risk. | Phase 6 / Phase 7 | Keep demand-driven explicit clear/hold activation; investigate reset semantics separately if needed. |
